# Slime env-balanced rollout sampler patch
# Generated: 2026-05-04 (wandb-metrics revision)
# Purpose: balance per-env fractions in each rollout batch when --env-sampling-weights set,
# with optional adaptive EMA-variance re-weighting (--env-sampling-adaptive), plus
# per-env telemetry (weights / draw counts / EMAs / variance) emitted to WandB
# under the env_sampler/* prefix so the user can watch the sampler live.
#
# Why: RLVR1_v2 dataset is IF-heavy. Bottom-reward envs (math, code_gen) get
# proportionally less gradient signal under GRPO/GSPO. Static weights fix the
# distribution; adaptive mode re-weights based on live reward feedback so
# saturated envs (pass rate ~1) get down-sampled and the learnable middle
# (pass rate ~0.5) gets up-sampled. The WandB metrics hook makes both modes
# observable — every rollout emits env_sampler/weight/<env>, draw_ratio/<env>,
# ema_reward/<env>, etc. See README.md "WandB metrics" for the full list.
#
# Apply with: git apply slime_env_balanced_sampler.patch
# NOTE: the rollout.py hunk assumes the NaN-mask patch (nan_masking.py) has
# been applied first. Apply order on a pod: nan_masking -> env_balanced_sampler.
#
